The Stage 2 peak selection, Stage 3 post-fit blend and Stage 1 anchor check
in this package come from anchorRefine (GPL-3). They were ported from the
following files at commit 55b9d09ba7e17b13e341e67b0aa03855351bc25b:

    R/anchor-check.R
    R/stage2-peaks.R
    R/stage2-search.R
    R/stage2-grid.R (peak-only dispatch)
    R/stage2-selected.R
    stage3/anchors.R

Source and license: https://github.com/amromeo/anchorRefine/tree/55b9d09ba7e17b13e341e67b0aa03855351bc25b

The peak search is derived from refineR 2.0.0 by Matthias Beck, Tatjana
Ammer, Christopher M Rank and Andre Schuetzenmeister, licensed GPL (>= 3).
The peak interpolation, smoothing and search regions derive from Tatjana
Ammer's findMainPeak, defineSearchRegions and related search code. The
vendored search, histogram and point-quantile functions are in
R/refiner_2_0_0.R with the original author notices. They come from
vendor/refineR/R/algoInvHist.R and vendor/refineR/R/utils.R at the Stage 0
revision above. The wrapper adapts findRI to the Box-Cox point-fit path.
The refineR code retains its GPL (>= 3) license. See
inst/licenses/refineR-GPL-3.txt for the license text. The anchorRefine
changes distributed here use GPL-3.

refineR source and license: https://cran.r-project.org/package=refineR
